{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0153pqh4sdYZ68K4biF6V7hd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n2\t# Sentry Error Monitoring\n3\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n4\t# Get your DSN from: https://sentry.io → Settings → Projects → <project> → Client Keys (DSN)\n5\tNEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0\n6\t\n7\t# Sentry auth token — used during `next build` to upload source maps.\n8\t# Generate at: https://sentry.io → Settings → Auth Tokens\n9\t# Add this to your CI secrets and Vercel/host environment variables (NOT committed).\n10\tSENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=\n11\t\n12\t# Optional: Override org/project slugs if different from sentry.properties\n13\t# SENTRY_ORG=your-org-slug\n14\t# SENTRY_PROJECT=your-project-slug\n15\t\n16\t# CSP violation reporting endpoint (Sentry Security Issues).\n17\t# Routes browser CSP violations to Sentry for forensic monitoring.\n18\t# Format: https://o<org-id>.ingest.sentry.io/api/<project-id>/security/?sentry_key=<public-key>\n19\t# Find it at: https://sentry.io → Settings → Projects → <project> → Security Headers\n20\t# Leave unset to disable violation reporting (CSP enforcement is unaffected).\n21\tSENTRY_CSP_REPORT_URI=\n22\t\n23\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n24\t# MOTAC Registration\n25\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n26\t# MOTAC tourist accommodation registration number (Malaysian law requirement).\n27\t# Displayed in footer, contact page, and JSON-LD structured data.\n28\tNEXT_PUBLIC_MOTAC_REG_NUMBER=\n29\t\n30\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n31\t# On-demand ISR Revalidation\n32\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n33\t# Shared secret for the /api/revalidate webhook endpoint.\n34\t# Generate a random string: openssl rand -hex 32\n35\t# Send it in the x-revalidate-secret header when calling the endpoint.\n36\tREVALIDATE_SECRET=\n37\t\n38\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n39\t# Stripe FPX Online Banking Payment\n40\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n41\t# Stripe account must be configured for Malaysia (MYR) with FPX payment method enabled.\n42\t# Get keys from: https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys\n43\tNEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...\n44\tSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...\n45\t\n46\t# Stripe webhook secret for /api/stripe-webhook endpoint.\n47\t# Create webhook at: https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks\n48\t# Events to listen for: payment_intent.succeeded, payment_intent.payment_failed\n49\tSTRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...\n50\t\n51\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n52\t# Channel Manager Integration (OTA Sync)\n53\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n54\t# Configure a channel manager (Beds24, Cloudbeds, SiteMinder) for:\n55\t# - Real-time ARI (Availability, Rate, Inventory) sync with OTAs\n56\t# - Webhook handling for booking updates from Booking.com, Agoda, Hostelworld\n57\t# - Prevention of overbookings across all distribution channels\n58\t\n59\t# Provider: \"beds24\" (recommended for small hostels)\n60\tCHANNEL_MANAGER_PROVIDER=beds24\n61\t\n62\t# Beds24 credentials\n63\t# Get from: https://www.beds24.com/ownersarea → API\n64\t# API Key: Account settings → API → API Key\n65\t# Property ID: Your Beds24 property ID (numeric)\n66\tBEDS24_API_KEY=\n67\tBEDS24_PROPERTY_ID=\n68\t\n69\t# Webhook validation secret (shared between website and channel manager)\n70\t# Set same value in your Beds24 webhook configuration\n71\t# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32\n72\tWEBHOOK_SECRET=\n73\t\n74\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n75\t# Local development overrides\n76\t# -------------------------------------------------------\n77\t# Uncomment to proxy Rainbow AI API to local server during dev\n78\t# RAINBOW_API_URL=http://localhost:3002\n79\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64023916-cf9d-44b1-9e84-df8466e38e83","uuid":"dc6f8525-2176-43bc-bd5d-9725f89adaff","timestamp":"2026-04-13T21:57:51.287Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\.env.local.example","content":"# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Sentry Error Monitoring\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Get your DSN from: https://sentry.io → Settings → Projects → <project> → Client Keys (DSN)\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0\n\n# Sentry auth token — used during `next build` to upload source maps.\n# Generate at: https://sentry.io → Settings → Auth Tokens\n# Add this to your CI secrets and Vercel/host environment variables (NOT committed).\nSENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=\n\n# Optional: Override org/project slugs if different from sentry.properties\n# SENTRY_ORG=your-org-slug\n# SENTRY_PROJECT=your-project-slug\n\n# CSP violation reporting endpoint (Sentry Security Issues).\n# Routes browser CSP violations to Sentry for forensic monitoring.\n# Format: https://o<org-id>.ingest.sentry.io/api/<project-id>/security/?sentry_key=<public-key>\n# Find it at: https://sentry.io → Settings → Projects → <project> → Security Headers\n# Leave unset to disable violation reporting (CSP enforcement is unaffected).\nSENTRY_CSP_REPORT_URI=\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# MOTAC Registration\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# MOTAC tourist accommodation registration number (Malaysian law requirement).\n# Displayed in footer, contact page, and JSON-LD structured data.\nNEXT_PUBLIC_MOTAC_REG_NUMBER=\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# On-demand ISR Revalidation\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Shared secret for the /api/revalidate webhook endpoint.\n# Generate a random string: openssl rand -hex 32\n# Send it in the x-revalidate-secret header when calling the endpoint.\nREVALIDATE_SECRET=\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Stripe FPX Online Banking Payment\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Stripe account must be configured for Malaysia (MYR) with FPX payment method enabled.\n# Get keys from: https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys\nNEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...\nSTRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...\n\n# Stripe webhook secret for /api/stripe-webhook endpoint.\n# Create webhook at: https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks\n# Events to listen for: payment_intent.succeeded, payment_intent.payment_failed\nSTRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Channel Manager Integration (OTA Sync)\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Configure a channel manager (Beds24, Cloudbeds, SiteMinder) for:\n# - Real-time ARI (Availability, Rate, Inventory) sync with OTAs\n# - Webhook handling for booking updates from Booking.com, Agoda, Hostelworld\n# - Prevention of overbookings across all distribution channels\n\n# Provider: \"beds24\" (recommended for small hostels)\nCHANNEL_MANAGER_PROVIDER=beds24\n\n# Beds24 credentials\n# Get from: https://www.beds24.com/ownersarea → API\n# API Key: Account settings → API → API Key\n# Property ID: Your Beds24 property ID (numeric)\nBEDS24_API_KEY=\nBEDS24_PROPERTY_ID=\n\n# Webhook validation secret (shared between website and channel manager)\n# Set same value in your Beds24 webhook configuration\n# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32\nWEBHOOK_SECRET=\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Local development overrides\n# -------------------------------------------------------\n# Uncomment to proxy Rainbow AI API to local server during dev\n# RAINBOW_API_URL=http://localhost:3002\n","numLines":79,"startLine":1,"totalLines":79}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BykxLyLEVWMBLuLxRkozRk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Now I have a good understanding of the structure. I can see that .env.local.example has all the configuration examples. I should add the Bing verification token there.\n\nNow let me create the implementation plan. Based on my analysis:\n\n## Current State\n- layout.tsx has metadata with Google verification token placeholder\n- .env.local.example has various configuration examples\n- sitemap.ts already generates a proper XML sitemap at /sitemap.xml\n- The project uses Next.js with TypeScript\n\n## Problem Identified\nThe site needs Bing Webmaster Tools verification to be added. Currently, only Google verification is configured. Need to:\n1. Add Bing verification token support to metadata\n2. Document how to configure it via environment variables\n3. Add the verification token to the meta tags\n\n## Planned Changes\n1. Update layout.tsx to:\n   - Import environment variable for Bing token\n   - Add Bing verification to the metadata.verification object using the token\n2. Update .env.local.example to:\n   - Add NEXT_PUBLIC_BING_VERIFICATION_TOKEN with instructions\n3. Create a step-by-step guide document for the manual parts (Bing account setup, submission, verification)\n\nWait, but I can't actually create the Bing account or submit the sitemap. The acceptance criteria ask for these things to be done. Let me reconsider what I should do.\n\nLooking at the acceptance criteria again:\n1. \"Bing Webmaster Tools account created at https://www.bing.com/webmasters/ and site verified\" - Manual action\n2. \"Verification via <meta name='msvalidate.01' content='TOKEN'> in layout.tsx metadata.verification\" - I can implement this\n3. \"Sitemap URL (https://pelangicapsulehostel.com/sitemap.xml) submitted to Bing\" - Manual action\n4. \"Bing crawl report shows pages indexed within 7 days of submission\" - Requires waiting\n\n\n5. \"No crawl errors reported in Bing Webmaster Tools dashboard\" - Requires manual verification\n\nThe reality is that some acceptance criteria require manual steps I can't perform. I should implement the code changes that enable Bing verification and provide clear documentation for the manual verification process. The human can then complete the account setup, submission, and verification steps once the code is deployed.\n\nLooking at the story requirements more carefully, creating a Bing Webmaster Tools account and verifying the site is a prerequisite before I can meaningfully test the meta tag implementation. However, I can validate that the meta tag renders correctly in the HTML using browser developer tools, which would at least confirm the technical implementation works. Let me check if there's already a Bing token in the actual environment configuration.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1285,"cache_read_input_tokens":84977,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1285},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64023916-cf9d-44b1-9e84-df8466e38e83","uuid":"0d864aa7-c564-4cf1-b0ba-f46de01ddd11"}
